Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-03-19T08:22:56Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T20:28:22Z","closed_at":"2026-03-19T15:24:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117617","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117617","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117617.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117617.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-19T15:24:14Z"},"body":"- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116169\r\n\r\nIt turns out this call was needed after all, it ensures new scripts are included in the global class list by updating EFS for them. In my previous PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108487) I must've only tested scripts that have been opened or loaded by the editor at some point so I didn't encounter the bug.\r\n\r\nThis reverts the https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108487 but with a deferred call to avoid reintroducing the bug that the PR fixed (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104052). Updating EFS here is still too early, so we defer the call to ensure the type info is available.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_u